# https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "18/12/2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "1) Factors that, if corrected, would likely have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm;2) Factors that if corrected, would not have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm, but are important for patient/staff safety or safe patient care in general (incidental findings); and3) Mitigating factors – factors that did not allow the incident to have more serious consequences and represent solid safeguards that should be kept in place.(Ref: Canadian Incident Analysis Framework – Canadian Patient Safety Institute 2012)" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Findings" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "1) Factors that, if corrected, would likely have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm;2) Factors that if corrected, would not have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm, but are important for patient/staff safety or safe patient care in general (incidental findings); and3) Mitigating factors – factors that did not allow the incident to have more serious consequences and represent solid safeguards that should be kept in place.(Ref: Canadian Incident Analysis Framework – Canadian Patient Safety Institute 2012)" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Findings" .
