<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "08/09/2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Rob" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Part 2/HSE Incident Management Framework/HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An event or circumstance which could have, or did, lead to unintended and/or unnecessary harm. Incidents include adverse events which result in harm; near-misses which could have resulted in harm, but did not cause harm, either by chance or timely intervention; and staff or service user complaints which are associated with harm." .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Incident" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "An event or circumstance which could have, or did, lead to unintended and/or unnecessary harm. Incidents include adverse events which result in harm; near-misses which could have resulted in harm, but did not cause harm, either by chance or timely intervention; and staff or service user complaints which are associated with harm." .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Incident" .
