# https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "18/12/2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The National Incident Report Form (NIRF) was developed by the State Claims Agency in conjunction with all stakeholders including the HSE and voluntary hospitals. Use of a NIRF assures the accuracy of data and clarity of information being reported. There are four forms in total; Person, Property, Crash/Collision and Dangerous Occurrences/Reportable Circumstance i.e. Dangerous Occurrences/Reportable Circumstances." .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "National Incident Reporting Form" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "The National Incident Report Form (NIRF) was developed by the State Claims Agency in conjunction with all stakeholders including the HSE and voluntary hospitals. Use of a NIRF assures the accuracy of data and clarity of information being reported. There are four forms in total; Person, Property, Crash/Collision and Dangerous Occurrences/Reportable Circumstance i.e. Dangerous Occurrences/Reportable Circumstances." .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#NationalIncidentReportingForm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "National Incident Reporting Form" .
