# 
# https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "18/12/2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Incident Management Framework 2020 / HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The term used nationally and internationally to describe the freedom from unnecessary harm or potential harm associated with healthcare services and the reduction of risk of unnecessary harm to an acceptable minimum (World Health Organisation, 2009). Where the term patient is used to describe ‘patient safety incident’, ‘quality and patient safety committees’ or ‘patient safety data’, it is intended to encompass all definitions of people who use health (including mental health) care services e.g. service users in both acute and community health care settings" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Patient Safety" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "The term used nationally and internationally to describe the freedom from unnecessary harm or potential harm associated with healthcare services and the reduction of risk of unnecessary harm to an acceptable minimum (World Health Organisation, 2009). Where the term patient is used to describe ‘patient safety incident’, ‘quality and patient safety committees’ or ‘patient safety data’, it is intended to encompass all definitions of people who use health (including mental health) care services e.g. service users in both acute and community health care settings" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafety> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Patient Safety" .
# 
# https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "18/12/2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The broad and heterogeneous information that includes, but is not limited to, the description of incidents with medical errors or near misses, their causes, the follow-up corrective actions, interventions that reduce future risk, and patient safety hazards." .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Patient safety data" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "The broad and heterogeneous information that includes, but is not limited to, the description of incidents with medical errors or near misses, their causes, the follow-up corrective actions, interventions that reduce future risk, and patient safety hazards." .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Patient safety data" .
# 
# https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "18/12/2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Incident Management Framework 2020" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A patient safety incident, in relation to the provision of a health service to a patient by a health services provider, means “an incident which occurs during the course of the provision of a health service”" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Patient Safety Incident" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "A patient safety incident, in relation to the provision of a health service to a patient by a health services provider, means “an incident which occurs during the course of the provision of a health service”" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#PatientSafetyIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Patient Safety Incident" .
